# FINAL PRODUCT EXPECTATION

The final product should demonstrate a functioning student-led classroom constitution process.

A student should be able to sign in, join a classroom, propose a right or duty, explain the reasoning, receive peer feedback, participate in formal voting, and see the proposal move to teacher review.

The teacher should be able to review the proposal and make a decision. If approved, the provision should become part of the classroom constitution.

Students should also be able to challenge existing practices through CIL and propose amendments to existing constitutional provisions while preserving historical versions.

The application should make the underlying educational idea immediately understandable to a middle-school student.

**Build a functional application, not just a visual mockup.**